<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rainulf Drengot</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1045</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rainulf Drengot was a Norman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary">mercenary</a> leader in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>. In 1030 Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sergius-iv-of-naples">Sergius IV of Naples</a> granted him Aversa to guard the frontier against Capua, making him the first Norman to hold a lordship in Italy. Aversa drew further Norman adventurers and became the springboard for the Norman conquest of the south.</p></div>
